/* H57.55CY: CX hardware proved that treating every physical VR hand as a
   blocker in the held-object predictive world query is wrong: one long hold
   produced thousands of "hand blocker" hits against the very hand anchoring
   the object.  CY keeps the native HPL query but classifies a VR hand wrapper
   relative to the held body: a hand currently gripping THIS body is self and
   ignored by the predictive sweep; the other/free hand remains a real solid
   blocker.  Simon/self + proven nonphysical Lux Area wrappers remain ignored.
   Unknown/external remains SOLID and H570 stays retired.  This changes only
   the predictive world qualifier; the Newton hand bodies/contact manifolds
   remain alive and solver-owned. */
